Nebula can route to a separately installed NVIDIA Personal AI Router on the same machine (shown in Nebula as a
Gravity upstream), and runs that router's backend services (built from its source, not included in this repository)
for model servers on your network. They are NVIDIA's, under the Apache License 2.0
(https://github.com/NVIDIA/Personal-AI-Router); a server bundle that carries them carries their LICENSE and NOTICE.

Halo's model files (nebula/assets/halo/) are LoRA adapters for Liquid AI's LFM2.5-1.2B-Instruct (Copyright Liquid AI),
modified by Nebula and distributed under the LFM Open License v1.0 (nebula/assets/halo/LICENSE-LFM-1.0); what was changed
is in nebula/assets/halo/README.md. The base model is not included: Nebula fetches Liquid's own file from its repository.

The installers carry llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml
authors): linked into Impulse's impulse-server, and its llama-server in halo/ as Halo's fallback runtime. Its licence
text is in app/LICENSE-llama.cpp and halo/LICENSE.

